Feature: New Ethereum Foundation Culture and Philosophy
  As a federated stabilizing board in a multi-polar ledger environment
  The New Ethereum Foundation rejects chain maximalism, enforces absolute treasury transparency, and promotes probabilistic routing

  Scenario: Public Compensation and Pay Packages Auditing
    Given a board member or core contributor is allocated compensation
    When the budget is synthesized
    Then the individual pay packages, denominated in native assets, must be publicly auditable on-chain
    And there must be no undisclosed compensation arrangements

  Scenario: Monerium SEPA-to-Crypto Stabilization Routing
    Given a network participant is a member of the federated stabilizing board
    When routing stabilization flows
    Then NEF should integrate corporate Monerium SEPA-to-Crypto vaults
    And it should route and settle transactions utilizing native assets or stablecoins to stabilize the manifold


  Scenario: Rejecting Chain Maximalism
    Given an ecosystem participant proposes a new ledger engine integration
    When the engine demonstrates real economic utility or validator topology decentralization
    Then the stabilizing board must treat the engine as a valid neighboring Manifold
    And the NEF must reject any proposal to arbitrarily restrict routing to a single preferred ledger
    And they align with the NEF multi-polar governance philosophy

  Scenario: Absolute Treasury Transparency
    Given the NEF treasury processes a funding grant or budget deployment
    When the transaction occurs
    Then the vault address, the authorized spenders, the approvers, and the code hash of the target contract must be published on-chain
    And there must be no shadow budgets or hidden reserves
    And they satisfy the NEF transparency charter

  Scenario: Collaborative Stability and Probabilistic Settlement
    Given network congestion or a localized liquidity crisis on a neighboring Manifold
    When routing transactions
    Then routing nodes should utilize probabilistic settlement pathways to bypass the congested route
    And they should prioritize system-wide liquidity preservation over isolationism
    And they align with the NEF global settlement vision

  Scenario: Probabilistic Settlement Evaluation
    Given the stabilizing board assesses the health of an active manifold
    When it retrieves the reported liquidity depth mesh
    Then it must evaluate manifold health using a probabilistic settlement score
    And it must adjust routing and stabilization weights based on the probability of successful settlement rather than simple block height metrics



